  In compiling Nethack 3.0 patchlevel 4 using Microsoft-C v5.1, I think 
I have found a bug in Nethack.  With TEXTCOLOR defined, all the monsters
show up as nice colors, which is fine.  However, when they first appear,
often they appear white, like the walls, and then after they take their
first step, they change into their normal color.  This seems like a bug
itself, but also, if you try to attack or name the creature when it is
white, the name is complete garbage, like an undefined pointer or
something.  

  Also, if you are hallucinated, the objects change color, but the monsters
seem to stay the same color.  So, if you see a monster, it will always
stay yellow, for example, even though it changes letters.

  Again, if anyone has compiled NH3.0 PL4 on MS-DOS, I'd be curious to
what options they included, what their final load size is (use EXEMOD from
MSC 5.1) and what they are running it under (DOS 3.3 with nnansi.sys, etc.).
I have a version which I was going to put up on lampwick.berkeley.edu, but
after playing it for a while, it sometimes bombs with not being able to
malloc memory, or it just hangs.  So, I guess I have to take out another
option (sigh.)....

